EmbodiedForge changes: local Python namespace; flat-only task registration and robot constants; repository-owned runtime, packaging and export entry; atomic checkpoint publication for local TensorBoard training; explicit ONNX export instead of automatic export on checkpoint saves; action-ordered export metadata with full-precision offsets/scales, replacing the shared MDP's global exporter patch.
The shared MDP helper module is retained without its global SDK patches. Nonfinite PPO advantages/returns now raise an error in a task-local PPO subclass rather than being replaced with zeros; reward handling uses mjlab 1.3.0's per-term implementation. Other upstream tasks are not registered.
Original code and asset paths/hashes are recorded in UPSTREAM.json.
Further local maintenance: retain the effective pose_target_match interface while removing its shadowed duplicate; give each SDK default entity selection a distinct named configuration; organize imports and types; exclude the right-hip bearing_roll body from head CoM randomization. The anatomical correction changes new training reset distributions and random-number consumption; historical implementation snapshots preserve the previous selection.
